			"description": "Deco Marquee v2 - Art Deco theatre portal: up to 5 fans (rays + rings), marquee bulbs and a closed ornament border, each element with its own color. Nothing moves by itself: drive Chase (0-1 = one step of the pattern, BPM Sync loops seamlessly), fan positions, fill, rotation or look from Arena. Each fan group (Fan 1-5) holds position and look of that fan. X \/ Y: 0 = screen center, -1 \/ 1 = fan center exactly on the screen edge (X left\/right, Y bottom\/top), -2 \/ 2 = fully outside. Z: 0 = normal size, higher = further away and smaller, also drawn behind nearer fans. Fill (deg) = how far the fan is open around its direction: 0 = fan off, 180 = half circle, 360 = full circle. Rotate (deg) = direction the fan opens to (0 = up). Ray Count = rays in a full circle (Fill reveals them), 0 = no rays; Ray Style Straight \/ Wedge (widening) \/ Long-Short. Ring Count 0 = no rings, fractional values fade the next ring in (FFT friendly); Ring Style Arch \/ Stepped \/ Chevron. Bulbs: Layout Rows \/ Frame \/ Arch (along the outer ring of fan 1); Bulb Inset = distance from the edge; Bulb Glow = halo of lit bulbs; Chase Mode Run (Chase Group bulbs per step, Chase Duty = lit share) \/ Alternate \/ Fill. Border: closed ornament band at the screen edge, Zigzag \/ Chevron \/ Steps. Backdrop On\/Off: colored background or transparent overlay. Drawn by the ISF shader DecoMarquee.fs in the patch folder (must stay next to the patch).",
			"displayName": "Deco Marquee v2",
